    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Simplifying surds means rewriting the surd in its simplest form. To do this, find the largest perfect square factor inside the square root and take its root outside the surd. For example, in <em>√12</em>, since 12 = 4 × 3 and 4 is a perfect square, <em>√12 = √4 × √3 = 2√3</em>.</p>",
